From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:44:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Add the ISP power states

The ISP's own power states are children of ISP_SYS at PMGR + 0x4000,
in the ADT's order: CPU, CPU cores 0 and 1, FE, DPRX, secure, STS0,
STS1, Pearl, BE, CLR, CVD and CVM, with the parents the ADT gives them.
The camera sensor power states ISPSENS0 and ISPSENS1 are at 0x188 and
0x190; the ADT lists both among the ISP's power gates.

Add them disabled, like ISP_SYS, and let the J713 policy enable them.
They have no consumer yet, so they stay off.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(backported from commit 47d8f59220ddf676a1d55edaf3877dd0b94dc82d)
[j604: J713 policy hunk (t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi) dropped: this tree has no J713 pmgr file and git's rename
 detection moved it onto t8132-j604-pmgr.dtsi. The J604 enables are a separate commit.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
